      },
      "message": "fix(3d): a pass restart in a 3D Pocket level takes the entry type\n\nA 3D Pocket pass that starts again inside a level after a hop (a zigzag\nrow on the far side of an island) went straight down at the plunge feed,\nalso when the entry was set to helix. The centre-cutting plunge law read\nthat restart only for a tool that does not cut at its centre.\n\nNow every restart is judged by plunge_law::into_solid. Into uncut stock,\na centre-cutting tool takes the entry type of the operation (helix,\nramp, arc), else the ramp along the pass, else the plunge with a note.\nEach candidate runs on a copy of the path and is kept only if it posts\nno plunge into solid and crosses no earlier move. A tool that does not\ncut at its centre keeps its M11.3 fallback. The catalog case\n3d/rough-finish is made again.\n\nFixes #3670\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
